WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:13.512
Choosing the right makeup format for the wedding parents makes all the difference to how they feel on the day and how happy they are with the result.

2
00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:18.720
Here's a comparison of on-site makeup and shop makeup.

3
00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:21.912
1) On-site makeup

4
00:00:22.248 --> 00:00:27.000
Pros: the biggest draw is the convenience of not having to travel.

5
00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:39.456
No need to lug a heavy hanbok bag to a shop on the wedding morning — the artist comes to your home or wherever you like, saving a lot of time and energy.

6
00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:48.312
Getting ready with family in a familiar space, with focused one-on-one attention, also brings emotional comfort.

7
00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:54.384
So it's convenient for parents with mobility issues or who live far away.

8
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.400
Cons: trust and legality are the biggest issues.

9
00:00:59.736 --> 00:01:06.216
About 85% of on-site artists currently working are unlicensed freelancers.

10
00:01:06.552 --> 00:01:14.328
They advertise and take bookings through social media, and customers, unaware of this, book without a second thought.

11
00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:23.184
Most on-site makeup services are either artists still building experience or unlicensed operations with no shop.

12
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.392
Surprising, right?

13
00:01:25.728 --> 00:01:28.560
"Can you issue a cash receipt?"

14
00:01:28.896 --> 00:01:40.296
If the answer is "Yes," that's at least reassuring, since it means they're registered as a business — but to be truly legitimate, they should have an actual shop or belong to a licensed one.

15
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:52.296
No-shows — artists who go silent or don't turn up on the day — happen from time to time, and given the gap in skill and experience, people say on-site makeup is a gamble.

16
00:01:52.632 --> 00:02:02.952
Unlike a shop, the products they can bring are limited, so without thorough prior consultation and preparation, quality can be hard to guarantee.

17
00:02:03.288 --> 00:02:05.904
2) Shop makeup

18
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.208
Pros: proven skill and full infrastructure.

19
00:02:11.544 --> 00:02:21.408
A veteran head artist or skilled specialist is likely on staff, meaning you can expect high-quality wedding-parent makeup.

20
00:02:21.744 --> 00:02:30.144
Every product is on hand to handle any situation, and the lighting and setting needed for makeup,

21
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:37.656
plus a licensed physical space, all add up to greater accountability and trust in the service.

22
00:02:37.992 --> 00:02:43.128
Cons: the hassle of travel and the risk of traffic.

23
00:02:43.464 --> 00:02:53.640
If the wedding is early, you'll need to head out early, and getting stuck in traffic can make you anxious — so building in extra time beforehand is key.
